# VIDEO-mode KEY frame byte-identity matrix, 72x88 q40, five synthetic
# content classes x twelve presets

date: 2026-09-01
host: mac (Apple aarch64), colima arm64 for the C-side --wrap dumps
base: ea23b52ad (docs(inter): §1l), i.e. the "before" column
after: the four chunks recorded in docs/INTER-ENCODE-PLAN.md §1m..§1p
       (the video palette ladder; the per-arm preset clamp on the dlf
        derivation; the per-arm `disallow_4x4` fork; and PD0_LVL_4 on the
        refinement path, with the subres transform-height fix to the PD0
        coefficient-rate threshold that it exposed)

## How it was produced

One build per column. Both sides encode the SAME 2-frame low-delay-P stream and
compare FRAME 0 only (the port refuses frame 1 and exits 3, which is the
expected state of the inter campaign, not a failure):

  port:  SVTAV1_FRAMES=2 SVTAV1_INTRA_PERIOD=64 SVTAV1_HIER_LEVELS=0 \
           identity_run <content> 72 88 40 <preset> <out>
  C:     SVT_FRAMES=2 SVT_INTRA_PERIOD=-1 SVT_HIER_LEVELS=0 SVT_PRED_STRUCT=1 \
           capture_c_trace 72 88 40 <preset> <port.yuv> <out.obu> 8

`c_bytes` is `c.obu.pts0`; `port_*` is `rs.obu.f0`. `verdict` is `cmp`, NOT the
percentage — a zero percentage is a SIZE claim, not a byte claim, and this
campaign has had a cell read 0.000 % while differing (see §1i's note on
`gradient 72x88 p9`). Read the verdict column.

## Result

42 -> 56 byte-identical of 60. Fourteen cells closed, one improved
(`gradient p3` 1.628 % -> 0.212 %), NOTHING worse and every cell the four
chunks cannot reach unchanged to the byte.

Closed: `screen` p7 + p8; all five content classes at p12 AND p13; `diag` p3;
`gradient` p8.

Still open: `gradient`/`diag`/`screenrep` at p0 (<= 0.483 %) and `gradient` p3
(0.212 %, coded tree exact — the residual is in the entropy layer). Nothing
above 0.5 % survives.
